How WebAssembly Works
Step 1

Write code in another language.

Example:

int multiply(int a, int b) {
    return a * b;
}

↓

Step 2

Compile into WASM.

multiply.cpp
      ↓
Compiler
      ↓
multiply.wasm

↓

Step 3

Load in browser.

JavaScript loads the .wasm file.

↓

Step 4

Execute.

Browser runs it efficiently.

Complete Flow

C/C++/Rust Code
        ↓
Compiler
        ↓
WebAssembly Binary (.wasm)
        ↓
Browser
        ↓
Execute